> Module Ctc_odc

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as QR
> Using Eitc as E

# Child tax credit, credit for other dependents, additional child tax credit (Schedule 8812; Form 1040 lines 19 and 28)

Issue #27, `scope.md` section 6.1. Direct File ("DF" below) module
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/ctcOdc.xml` (1596
lines, read in full) and the per-person facts
`/familyAndHousehold/*/ssnValidForEmployment`, `/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleCtc`
and `/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleOdc` of `familyAndHousehold.xml` (lines
3756-3920). Law: 26 U.S.C. § 24 (`sources/statute/irc-24.html`, U.S. Code 2024
edition); Treas. Reg. § 1.24-1 (`sources/regs/cfr-1.24-1.xml`); Rev. Proc.
2023-34 § 3.05 (`sources/revproc/rp-23-34.pdf` p 8); Schedule 8812 (Form 1040)
2024 (`sources/forms-instructions/f1040s8--2024.pdf`, 2 pp) and its
instructions (`sources/forms-instructions/i1040s8--2024.pdf`, 9 pp; Credit
Limit Worksheet A on p 4, Earned Income Chart on p 7).

The module has three scopes.

- `CtcOdcPersonTest`: one member of the household. It runs the dependent
  tests of `Qualifying_relative.DependentTest` (issue #17, which itself runs
  `Qualifying_child.QualifyingChildTest`, issue #16) and adds the two
  credit-specific tests: is the person a qualifying child for the child tax
  credit (DF `eligibleCtc`), or a dependent for the credit for other
  dependents (DF `eligibleOdc`).
- `CtcOdcDependents`: the same test mapped over the household, and the two
  counts, Schedule 8812 lines 4 and 6 (DF `/ctcEligibleDependents`,
  `/odcEligibleDependents`).
- `Schedule8812`: Schedule 8812 Parts I and II, from the two counts and the
  return figures. Outputs `total_ctc_and_odc` (line 14, Form 1040 line 19)
  and `additional_ctc` (line 27, Form 1040 line 28).

The return figures are inputs (CONVENTIONS sections 2 and 7): the order in
which credits are taken (scope.md section 6.7) puts the CTC and ODC last
among the nonrefundable credits, and the additional child tax credit after
the earned income credit, which it reads. Each input names the module that
computes it; the wiring is listed in the pull request.

Tests: `catala/tests/test_ctc_odc.catala_en`. Oracle comparison:
`make difftest SCOPE=ctc_odc` (Schedule 8812 from the oracle's counts) and
`make difftest SCOPE=ctc_odc_household` (the counts from the household
members), against `oracle/facts.csv`; `make difftest-persons` (scope
`ctc_odc_person`, each person against `oracle/persons.csv`).

Not here, on purpose: Form 8862 (information to claim the credit after a
disallowance), which DF fills in and this module only flags
(`ctc8862_required`); Credit Limit Worksheet B (needed only with the mortgage
interest, adoption, residential clean energy or D.C. homebuyer credits, which
DF does not support); Puerto Rico residents and Form 2555 filers (DF scope);
the line 15 box "do not want to claim the additional child tax credit"
(DF has no such question). The PDF-only facts (`/pdf8812...`) are not
modelled (CONVENTIONS section 2).

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## IRC 24(c)(1): a qualifying child "who has not attained age 17". Not
## indexed. DF: `familyAndHousehold.xml` `/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleCtc`
## (`age` less than `17`).
declaration ctc_age_limit content integer equals 17

## IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(ii): "in the case of a taxpayer with 3 or more qualifying
## children". Schedule 8812 line 20 asks the same thing as "On line 16b, is
## the amount $5,100 or more?" ($5,100 = 3 x $1,700).
## DF: `/threeOrMoreCtcEligibleDependents` (`GreaterThanOrEqual` `3`).
declaration actc_alternative_minimum_children content integer equals 3

## What the person's Social Security card says about employment. DF:
## `familyAndHousehold.xml` `/familyAndHouseholdSsnEmploymentValidityOptions`
## (lines 20-31), one constructor per option, same order. `Neither` is a card
## with no restriction printed on it.
declaration enumeration SsnEmploymentValidity:
  -- Neither
  -- NotValid
  -- ValidOnlyWithDhsAuthorizationInEffect
  -- ValidOnlyWithDhsAuthorizationExpired

## One member of DF `/familyAndHousehold`, with the one answer the CTC reads
## beyond those of `Qualifying_relative.Member`.
declaration structure HouseholdMember:
  data member content QR.Member
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/ssnEmploymentValidity. DF asks it of persons
  # with an SSN; for anybody else the value is never read.
  data ssn_employment_validity content SsnEmploymentValidity
```

## One person: who counts for which credit

```catala-metadata
declaration scope CtcOdcPersonTest:
  # One member of DF /familyAndHousehold
  input household_member content HouseholdMember
  # DF: filers.xml /minimumFilerDateOfBirth (Filers.minimum_filer_date_of_birth)
  input minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents (Filers.treat_filers_as_dependents)
  input treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  # DF: filers.xml /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  # (Filers.either_filer_us_citizen_or_national)
  input either_filer_us_citizen_or_national content boolean
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ (Filers.treat_as_mfj); read only by the
  # benefit-split scope that DependentTest runs (issue #18)
  input treat_as_mfj content boolean

  # The dependent tests for the same person (issue #17)
  output dependent content QR.DependentTest
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/ssnValidForEmployment
  output ssn_valid_for_employment condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleCtc
  output eligible_ctc condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleOdc
  output eligible_odc condition
```

```catala
scope CtcOdcPersonTest:
  definition dependent equals
    output of QR.DependentTest with {
      -- member: household_member.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: minimum_filer_date_of_birth
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: treat_filers_as_dependents
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national:
           either_filer_us_citizen_or_national
      -- treat_as_mfj: treat_as_mfj }
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(a) and (c): the qualifying child

IRC 24(a): "There shall be allowed as a credit against the tax imposed by this
chapter for the taxable year with respect to each qualifying child of the
taxpayer for which the taxpayer is allowed a deduction under section 151 an
amount equal to $1,000." So the child must be claimed: DF
`/familyAndHousehold/*/isClaimedDependent` (the filer chose to claim an
eligible dependent; `Qualifying_relative`).

IRC 24(c)(1): "The term "qualifying child" means a qualifying child of the
taxpayer (as defined in section 152(c)) who has not attained age 17." DF
`qualifyingChild` (`Qualifying_child`) and `age` less than 17, where `age` is
2024 minus the year of birth, the age on December 31, 2024. The Schedule 8812
instructions (`i1040s8--2024.pdf` p 2), "Credits for Qualifying Children":
"the child must be your dependent, under age 17 at the end of 2024", and
"Example 1. Your child turned 17 on December 30, 2024, ... You can't use the
child to claim the CTC or ACTC because the child was not under age 17 at the
end of 2024." A child born on December 31, 2007 is 17 at the end of 2024 and
does not count; a child born on January 1, 2008 is 16 and counts (the
"day before the birthday" rule used for some other ages, scope.md section
5.1, is not the rule here).

IRC 24(c)(2): "The term "qualifying child" shall not include any individual
who would not be a dependent if subparagraph (A) of section 152(b)(3) were
applied without regard to all that follows "resident of the United States"."
That is the citizen or resident test without the Canada and Mexico residents;
the adopted-child exception of 152(b)(3)(B) still applies, because only
subparagraph (A) is cut. DF `/familyAndHousehold/*/citizenOrUsResidentTest`
(`Qualifying_relative.citizen_or_us_resident_test`: citizen, U.S. resident,
U.S. national, or the adopted-child exception).

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(h)(7): the required Social Security number

IRC 24(h)(7): "No credit shall be allowed under this section to a taxpayer
with respect to any qualifying child unless the taxpayer includes the social
security number of such child on the return of tax for the taxable year. For
purposes of the preceding sentence, the term "social security number" means a
social security number issued to an individual by the Social Security
Administration, but only if the social security number is issued— (A) to a
citizen of the United States or pursuant to subclause (I) (or that portion of
subclause (III) that relates to subclause (I)) of section 205(c)(2)(B)(i) of
the Social Security Act, and (B) before the due date for such return."

Schedule 8812 instructions p 1, "Each Qualifying Child You Use for CTC or
ACTC Must Have the Required SSN": "The required SSN is one that is valid for
employment and is issued before the due date of your 2024 return (including
extensions)." DF: the TIN is an SSN (`tinType` = `ssn`) and
`ssnValidForEmployment`: the card says neither "Not valid for employment" nor
"Valid for work only with DHS authorization" with the authorization expired.
DF has no question about the issue date; an SSN entered on the return is
taken as issued in time.

```catala
scope CtcOdcPersonTest:
  # IRC 24(h)(7); i1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/ssnValidForEmployment
  rule ssn_valid_for_employment under condition
    household_member.ssn_employment_validity = Neither
    or household_member.ssn_employment_validity
       = ValidOnlyWithDhsAuthorizationInEffect
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(a), 24(c)(1), 24(c)(2), 24(h)(7); i1040s8--2024.pdf pp 1-2.
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleCtc
  rule eligible_ctc under condition
    dependent.is_claimed_dependent
    and dependent.qualifying_child
    and dependent.qc.age < ctc_age_limit
    and dependent.citizen_or_us_resident_test
    and household_member.member.answers.tin_type = QR.TinType.Ssn
    and ssn_valid_for_employment
  consequence fulfilled
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(h)(4): the credit for other dependents

IRC 24(h)(4)(A): "The credit determined under subsection (a) (after the
application of paragraph (2)) shall be increased by $500 for each dependent of
the taxpayer (as defined in section 152) other than a qualifying child
described in subsection (c)." Treas. Reg. § 1.24-1(a) says the same: "a
taxpayer may be eligible to increase the credit determined under section
24(a) by $500 for a dependent of the taxpayer, as defined in section 152,
other than a qualifying child described in section 24(c)."

IRC 24(h)(4)(B): "Subparagraph (A) shall not apply with respect to any
individual who would not be a dependent if subparagraph (A) of section
152(b)(3) were applied without regard to all that follows "resident of the
United States"." The same citizen or U.S. resident test as 24(c)(2).

IRC 24(h)(4)(C): "In the case of any qualifying child with respect to whom a
credit is not allowed under this section by reason of paragraph (7), such
child shall be treated as a dependent to whom subparagraph (A) applies."

Schedule 8812 line 6 (`f1040s8--2024.pdf` p 1): "Number of other dependents,
including any qualifying children who are not under age 17 or who do not have
the required social security number ... Caution: Do not include yourself,
your spouse, or anyone who is not a U.S. citizen, U.S. national, or U.S.
resident alien. Also, do not include anyone you included on line 4."
Instructions p 2, "Credit for Other Dependents (ODC)": "1. The person is
claimed as a dependent on your return. ... 2. The person can't be used by you
to claim the CTC or ACTC. ... 3. The person was a U.S. citizen, U.S. national,
or U.S. resident alien. ... If the person is your adopted child, see Adopted
child". Instructions p 1: a dependent with no SSN, ITIN or ATIN can't be used
for the ODC; `Qualifying_relative.eligible_dependent` already requires a TIN.

DF `/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleOdc`: claimed, not `eligibleCtc`, and
`citizenOrUsResidentTest`. "Not eligible for the CTC" covers both the
dependent who is not a qualifying child under 17 and, by (h)(4)(C), the
qualifying child under 17 without the required SSN.

```catala
scope CtcOdcPersonTest:
  # IRC 24(h)(4)(A)-(C); Treas. Reg. 1.24-1(a); Sch 8812 line 6,
  # f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1; i1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleOdc
  rule eligible_odc under condition
    dependent.is_claimed_dependent
    and not eligible_ctc
    and dependent.citizen_or_us_resident_test
  consequence fulfilled
```

## The household: Schedule 8812 lines 4 and 6

Schedule 8812 line 4: "Number of qualifying children under age 17 with the
required social security number"; line 6: "Number of other dependents"
(text above). Instructions p 2: "You can't check both the child tax credit
box and the credit for other dependents box for the same person." The two
tests above exclude each other (`eligible_odc` requires `not eligible_ctc`).

DF `/ctcEligibleDependents` and `/odcEligibleDependents` count
`/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleCtc` and `/familyAndHousehold/*/eligibleOdc`.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope CtcOdcDependents:
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold
  input household_members content list of HouseholdMember
  # DF: filers.xml /minimumFilerDateOfBirth
  input minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents
  input treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  # DF: filers.xml /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  input either_filer_us_citizen_or_national content boolean
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ
  input treat_as_mfj content boolean

  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/... (one result per member, same order)
  output results content list of CtcOdcPersonTest
  # Sch 8812 line 4. DF: /ctcEligibleDependents
  output ctc_eligible_dependents content integer
  # Sch 8812 line 6. DF: /odcEligibleDependents
  output odc_eligible_dependents content integer
```

```catala
scope CtcOdcDependents:
  definition results equals
    map each m among household_members to
      (output of CtcOdcPersonTest with {
         -- household_member: m
         -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: minimum_filer_date_of_birth
         -- treat_filers_as_dependents: treat_filers_as_dependents
         -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national:
              either_filer_us_citizen_or_national
         -- treat_as_mfj: treat_as_mfj })

  # Sch 8812 line 4, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1. DF: /ctcEligibleDependents
  definition ctc_eligible_dependents equals
    number of (list of r among results such that r.eligible_ctc)

  # Sch 8812 line 6, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1. DF: /odcEligibleDependents
  definition odc_eligible_dependents equals
    number of (list of r among results such that r.eligible_odc)
```

## Schedule 8812

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Schedule8812:
  # ---- Household (CtcOdcDependents) ----
  # Sch 8812 line 4. DF: /ctcEligibleDependents
  input ctc_eligible_dependents content integer
  # Sch 8812 line 6. DF: /odcEligibleDependents
  input odc_eligible_dependents content integer

  # ---- Return figures ----
  # DF: /filingStatus (only "is it MFJ" is read: filingStatus.xml /isFilingStatusMFJ)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # Form 1040 line 11. DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi (Form_1040)
  input agi content money
  # Form 1040 line 18. DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalTentativeTax (Form_1040)
  input total_tentative_tax content money
  # Schedule 3 line 2. DF: cdcc.xml /cdccTotalCredit (CDCC, issue #28)
  input cdcc_total_credit content money
  # Schedule 3 line 4. DF: saversCredits.xml /qualifiedSaverCreditAmount
  # (Savers_credit, issue #29)
  input qualified_saver_credit_amount content money
  # Schedule 3 line 6d. DF: elderlyAndDisabled.xml /totalEdc
  # (Elderly_and_disabled, issue #30)
  input total_edc content money
  # Form 1040 line 1z. DF: income.xml /employerIncomeSubtotal (Form_1040)
  input employer_income_subtotal content money
  # Nontaxable combat pay of both filers, Sch 8812 line 18b.
  # DF: formW2s.xml /allCombatPay (Form_w2s.FormW2s.all_combat_pay)
  input all_combat_pay content money
  # W-2 boxes 4 and 6, Sch 8812 line 21.
  # DF: formW2s.xml /socialSecurityTaxesWithheld
  # (Form_w2s.FormW2s.social_security_taxes_withheld)
  input social_security_taxes_withheld content money
  # Form 1040 line 27. DF: eitc.xml /earnedIncomeCredit
  # (Eitc.EarnedIncomeCredit.earned_income_credit)
  input earned_income_credit content money

  # ---- Improper claims (IRC 24(g)) ----
  # DF: /receivedImproperClaims
  input received_improper_claims content boolean
  # DF: /receivedImproperClaimsNotice (options /improperClaimsNoticeOptions)
  input received_improper_claims_notice content E.ImproperClaimsNotice
  # DF: /improperClaimsNoticeExpired
  input improper_claims_notice_expired content boolean
  # DF: /hasFiledCtcOdcSinceNoticeExpired
  input has_filed_ctc_odc_since_notice_expired content boolean

  # DF: /hadCtcOdcImproperClaimsBan
  output had_ctc_odc_improper_claims_ban condition
  # DF: /ctcOdcDisqualifiedForImproperClaims
  output ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims condition

  # ---- Part I ----
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForCtc
  output maybe_eligible_for_ctc condition
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForOdc
  output maybe_eligible_for_odc condition
  # DF: /ctcQualified
  output ctc_qualified condition
  # DF: /odcQualified
  output odc_qualified condition
  # Sch 8812 line 3. DF: /dependentCreditMagi
  output dependent_credit_magi content money
  # Sch 8812 line 5. DF: /totalPotentialCtc
  output total_potential_ctc content money
  # Sch 8812 line 7. DF: /totalPotentialOdc
  output total_potential_odc content money
  # Sch 8812 line 8. DF: /totalPotentialDependentCredits
  output total_potential_dependent_credits content money
  # Sch 8812 line 9. DF: /dependentCreditPhaseoutThreshold
  output dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold content money
  # Line 3 minus line 9, not below zero. DF: /dependentCreditMagiAboveThreshold
  output dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold content money
  # Sch 8812 line 10. DF: /roundedDependentCreditMagiAboveThreshold
  output rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold content money
  # Sch 8812 line 11. DF: /dependentCreditPhaseout
  output dependent_credit_phaseout content money
  # Sch 8812 line 12. DF: /dependentCreditLessPhaseout
  output dependent_credit_less_phaseout content money
  # Sch 8812 line 12 "Yes" box. DF: /dependentCreditNotFullyPhasedOut
  output dependent_credit_not_fully_phased_out condition
  # Sch 8812 line 13 (Credit Limit Worksheet A line 5). DF: /sched8812CreditLimit
  output sched8812_credit_limit content money
  # Sch 8812 line 14, Form 1040 line 19. DF: /totalCtcAndOdc
  output total_ctc_and_odc content money
  # DF: /maxPotentialOdcAfterPhaseOut
  output max_potential_odc_after_phase_out content money
  # The ODC part of line 14 (no form line). DF: /totalOdc
  output total_odc content money
  # The CTC part of line 14 (no form line). DF: /totalCtc
  output total_ctc content money
  # DF: /isReceivingCtc
  output is_receiving_ctc condition
  # DF: /isReceivingOdc
  output is_receiving_odc condition
  # DF: /isReceivingCtcOrOdc
  output is_receiving_ctc_or_odc condition

  # ---- Part II-A ----
  # Sch 8812 line 16a. DF: /remainingCtcAndOdc
  output remaining_ctc_and_odc content money
  # DF: /xmlHasRemainingCtcAndOdc
  output xml_has_remaining_ctc_and_odc condition
  # Sch 8812 line 16b. DF: /totalPotentialActc
  output total_potential_actc content money
  # DF: /xmlHasPotentialActc
  output xml_has_potential_actc condition
  # Sch 8812 line 17. DF: /remainingPotentialActc
  output remaining_potential_actc content money
  # Sch 8812 line 18a. DF: income.xml /earnedIncomeWithAllCombatPay
  output earned_income_with_all_combat_pay content money
  # Sch 8812 line 19. DF: /earnedIncomeAboveActcRefundabilityThreshold
  output earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold content money
  # Sch 8812 line 19 "Yes" box. DF: /earnedIncomeExceedsActcRefundabilityThreshold
  output earned_income_exceeds_actc_refundability_threshold condition
  # Sch 8812 line 20. DF: /regularMaximumActc
  output regular_maximum_actc content money
  # Sch 8812 line 20 "Next" question (line 16b at least $5,100).
  # DF: /threeOrMoreCtcEligibleDependents
  output three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents condition
  # DF: /xmlThreeOrMoreCtcEligibleDependents
  output xml_three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents condition

  # ---- Part II-B ----
  # Sch 8812 line 25. DF: /socialSecurityOverEitc
  output social_security_over_eitc content money
  # Sch 8812 line 26 (or line 20 when Part II-B is skipped). DF: /maximumActc
  output maximum_actc content money

  # ---- Part II-C ----
  # Sch 8812 line 27, Form 1040 line 28. DF: /additionalCtc
  output additional_ctc content money
  # DF: /isReceivingActc
  output is_receiving_actc condition
  # DF: /ctc8862Required
  output ctc8862_required condition
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(g): taxpayers who improperly claimed the credit

IRC 24(g)(1)(A): "No credit shall be allowed under this section for any
taxable year in the disallowance period." (g)(1)(B): "the disallowance period
is— (i) the period of 10 taxable years after the most recent taxable year for
which there was a final determination that the taxpayer's claim of credit
under this section was due to fraud, and (ii) the period of 2 taxable years
after the most recent taxable year for which there was a final determination
that the taxpayer's claim of credit under this section was due to reckless or
intentional disregard of rules and regulations (but not due to fraud)."
IRC 24(g)(2): "In the case of a taxpayer who is denied credit under this
section for any taxable year as a result of the deficiency procedures under
subchapter B of chapter 63, no credit shall be allowed under this section for
any subsequent taxable year unless the taxpayer provides such information as
the Secretary may require to demonstrate eligibility for such credit."

Schedule 8812 instructions p 2, "Improper Claims": "If you erroneously claim
the CTC, ACTC, or ODC and it is later determined that your error was due to
reckless or intentional disregard of the CTC, ACTC, or ODC rules, you will not
be allowed to claim any of these credits for 2 years ... If it is determined
that your error was due to fraud, you will not be allowed to claim any of
these credits for 10 years." "Form 8862 may be required. If your CTC ...,
ACTC, or ODC for a year after 2015 was denied or reduced for any reason other
than a math or clerical error, you must attach Form 8862 to your tax return to
claim the CTC, ACTC, or ODC unless an exception applies."

DF asks whether the credit was reduced or disallowed (`receivedImproperClaims`),
for how many years the IRS letter barred it (`receivedImproperClaimsNotice`:
2, 10 or 0 years), whether that period is over (`improperClaimsNoticeExpired`)
and whether the filer has claimed the credit since it ended
(`hasFiledCtcOdcSinceNoticeExpired`). A filer still inside a 2- or 10-year
period gets no CTC, ODC or ACTC (`ctcOdcDisqualifiedForImproperClaims`: lines
5, 7 and 16b are `$0`); a filer whose period is over and who has not claimed
since, or whose letter set no period, must attach Form 8862
(`ctc8862Required`). Both match the statute.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # DF: /hadCtcOdcImproperClaimsBan
  rule had_ctc_odc_improper_claims_ban under condition
    not has_filed_ctc_odc_since_notice_expired
    and (received_improper_claims_notice = E.ImproperClaimsNotice.TwoYears
         or received_improper_claims_notice = E.ImproperClaimsNotice.TenYears)
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(g)(1); i1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /ctcOdcDisqualifiedForImproperClaims
  rule ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims under condition
    received_improper_claims
    and not has_filed_ctc_odc_since_notice_expired
    and had_ctc_odc_improper_claims_ban
    and not improper_claims_notice_expired
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(g)(2); i1040s8--2024.pdf p 2. DF: /ctc8862Required
  rule ctc8862_required under condition
    (is_receiving_ctc or is_receiving_actc or is_receiving_odc)
    and received_improper_claims
    and not has_filed_ctc_odc_since_notice_expired
    and ((had_ctc_odc_improper_claims_ban and improper_claims_notice_expired)
         or received_improper_claims_notice
            = E.ImproperClaimsNotice.ZeroYears)
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Part I, lines 4 to 8: the credit before the phase-out

IRC 24(h)(2): "Subsection (a) shall be applied by substituting "$2,000" for
"$1,000"." (`P.ctc_per_qualifying_child`). IRC 24(h)(4)(A): "increased by
$500 for each dependent" (`P.odc_per_other_dependent`). Schedule 8812 line 5:
"Multiply line 4 by $2,000"; line 7: "Multiply line 6 by $500"; line 8: "Add
lines 5 and 7".

DF `/totalPotentialCtc`, `/totalPotentialOdc`: `$0` when the filer is
disqualified under 24(g) or has no such dependent, else the count times the
amount, rounded (a no-op on whole dollars).

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForCtc
  rule maybe_eligible_for_ctc under condition ctc_eligible_dependents > 0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: /maybeEligibleForOdc
  rule maybe_eligible_for_odc under condition odc_eligible_dependents > 0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: /ctcQualified
  rule ctc_qualified under condition
    not ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims and maybe_eligible_for_ctc
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: /odcQualified
  rule odc_qualified under condition
    not ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims and maybe_eligible_for_odc
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(a), 24(h)(2), 24(g)(1); Sch 8812 line 5, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /totalPotentialCtc
  definition total_potential_ctc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims or not maybe_eligible_for_ctc
       then $0
       else P.ctc_per_qualifying_child * (decimal of ctc_eligible_dependents))

  # IRC 24(h)(4)(A), 24(g)(1); Sch 8812 line 7, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /totalPotentialOdc
  definition total_potential_odc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims or not maybe_eligible_for_odc
       then $0
       else P.odc_per_other_dependent * (decimal of odc_eligible_dependents))

  # Sch 8812 line 8, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1. DF: /totalPotentialDependentCredits
  definition total_potential_dependent_credits equals
    R.round_dollar of (total_potential_ctc + total_potential_odc)
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(b)(1) and (h)(3): the phase-out, lines 1 to 3 and 9 to 12

IRC 24(b)(1): "The amount of the credit allowable under subsection (a) shall
be reduced (but not below zero) by $50 for each $1,000 (or fraction thereof)
by which the taxpayer's modified adjusted gross income exceeds the threshold
amount. For purposes of the preceding sentence, the term "modified adjusted
gross income" means adjusted gross income increased by any amount excluded
from gross income under section 911, 931, or 933." IRC 24(h)(3): "In lieu of
the amount determined under subsection (b)(2), the threshold amount shall be
$400,000 in the case of a joint return ($200,000 in any other case)."

Schedule 8812 line 1: "Enter the amount from line 11 of your Form 1040"; lines
2a to 2c (Puerto Rico income, Form 2555, Form 4563) are `$0` in DF's scope, so
line 3 is the AGI (DF `/dependentCreditMagi`, whose description says so).
Line 9: "Married filing jointly—$400,000; All other filing statuses—$200,000".
A qualifying surviving spouse does not file a joint return and uses $200,000.
Line 10: "Subtract line 9 from line 3. If zero or less, enter -0-. If more
than zero and not a multiple of $1,000, enter the next multiple of $1,000. For
example, if the result is $425, enter $1,000; if the result is $1,025, enter
$2,000, etc." Line 11: "Multiply line 10 by 5% (0.05)". Line 12: "Is the
amount on line 8 more than the amount on line 11? No. STOP. You cannot take
the child tax credit, credit for other dependents, or additional child tax
credit. ... Yes. Subtract line 11 from line 8."

**Rounding up to the next $1,000.** DF `/roundedDependentCreditMagiAboveThreshold`
is `Round(StepwiseMultiply(excess + 999.99, 1000/1000))`: add $999.99, drop
the cents, keep the whole thousands. The excess is a whole number of dollars
(line 3 is rounded), so this is the next multiple of $1,000 at or above the
excess, as line 10 says ($0 stays $0, $1 gives $1,000, $1,000 gives $1,000,
$1,001 gives $2,000). We use `R.stepwise_multiply` exactly as DF does, with
`$999.99` written as the step less one cent. `Money.round_to_decimal` is not
used: Catala rounds half away from zero there, so it would need a different
offset, and the convention is to mirror DF's operator (CONVENTIONS section 4).
Line 11 is line 10 times $50 / $1,000 = 5%, exact on a multiple of $1,000.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # IRC 24(b)(1); Sch 8812 lines 1-3, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /dependentCreditMagi
  definition dependent_credit_magi equals R.round_dollar of agi

  # IRC 24(h)(3); Sch 8812 line 9, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /dependentCreditPhaseoutThreshold
  definition dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold equals
    if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    then P.ctc_phaseout_threshold_joint
    else P.ctc_phaseout_threshold_other

  # IRC 24(b)(1) "exceeds the threshold amount".
  # DF: /dependentCreditMagiAboveThreshold
  definition dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold equals
    Money.positive of (dependent_credit_magi - dependent_credit_phaseout_threshold)

  # IRC 24(b)(1) "for each $1,000 (or fraction thereof)"; Sch 8812 line 10,
  # f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /roundedDependentCreditMagiAboveThreshold
  # (Round(StepwiseMultiply(excess + 999.99, 1000/1000)))
  definition rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (R.stepwise_multiply of
         (dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold + P.ctc_phaseout_step - $0.01),
         1000, 1000)

  # IRC 24(b)(1) "$50 for each $1,000"; Sch 8812 line 11, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /dependentCreditPhaseout (Round(line 10 x 5/100))
  definition dependent_credit_phaseout equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (rounded_dependent_credit_magi_above_threshold
       * (P.ctc_phaseout_reduction_per_step / P.ctc_phaseout_step))

  # IRC 24(b)(1) "(but not below zero)"; Sch 8812 line 12, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1.
  # DF: /dependentCreditLessPhaseout
  definition dependent_credit_less_phaseout equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.positive of (total_potential_dependent_credits - dependent_credit_phaseout))

  # Sch 8812 line 12 "Yes". DF: /dependentCreditNotFullyPhasedOut
  rule dependent_credit_not_fully_phased_out under condition
    dependent_credit_less_phaseout > $0
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Lines 13 and 14: the credit limit (Credit Limit Worksheet A)

IRC 24 allows the credit "against the tax imposed by this chapter"; the
nonrefundable credits of subpart A together may not exceed the tax (IRC
26(a)), and the CTC and ODC are taken after the other credits on Schedule 3.
Credit Limit Worksheet A (`i1040s8--2024.pdf` p 4): "1. Enter the amount from
line 18 of your Form 1040 ... 2. Add the following amounts (if applicable)
from: Schedule 3, line 1 ... line 2 ... line 3 ... line 4 ... line 5b ...
line 6d ... line 6f ... line 6l ... line 6m ... 3. Subtract line 2 from line
1. ... 4. If you are not completing Credit Limit Worksheet B, enter -0-;
otherwise, enter the amount from Credit Limit Worksheet B. 5. Subtract line 4
from line 3. Enter here and on Schedule 8812, line 13." Schedule 8812 line 14:
"Enter the smaller of line 12 or line 13. This is your child tax credit and
credit for other dependents ... Enter this amount on Form 1040 ... line 19."

DF `/sched8812CreditLimit`: `GreaterOf(0, totalTentativeTax - (sched3Line1 +
cdccTotalCredit + sched3Line3 + qualifiedSaverCreditAmount + sched3Line5b +
totalEdc + sched3Line6f + sched3Line6l + sched3Line6m))`. Of the nine
Schedule 3 lines only line 2 (child and dependent care credit, #28), line 4
(retirement savings contributions credit, #29) and line 6d (credit for the
elderly or disabled, #30) are in DF's scope; the others are `<!-- PLACEHOLDER
-->` facts held at `$0` (foreign tax credit, education credits, residential
energy, and the 6f, 6l, 6m lines). Worksheet B is "OUT OF SCOPE" in DF (its
four credits are not supported), so line 4 is `$0`. The `GreaterOf(0, ...)`
is not on the worksheet, but the three credits are each limited to the tax
left before them (scope.md section 6.7), so line 3 cannot be negative; the
floor changes nothing.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # OUT OF SCOPE: Schedule 3 lines 1, 3, 5b, 6f, 6l, 6m are $0 placeholders
  # in DF (their credits are not supported), and Credit Limit Worksheet B
  # (line 4) is out of scope.
  # Credit Limit Worksheet A lines 1-5, i1040s8--2024.pdf p 4; Sch 8812 line 13.
  # DF: /sched8812CreditLimit
  definition sched8812_credit_limit equals
    Money.positive of
      (total_tentative_tax
       - (cdcc_total_credit + qualified_saver_credit_amount + total_edc))

  # IRC 24(a), 26(a); Sch 8812 line 14, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 1; Form 1040 line 19.
  # DF: /totalCtcAndOdc
  definition total_ctc_and_odc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.min of dependent_credit_less_phaseout, sched8812_credit_limit)

  # DF: /isReceivingCtcOrOdc
  rule is_receiving_ctc_or_odc under condition total_ctc_and_odc > $0
  consequence fulfilled
```

**The split of line 14 between CTC and ODC.** Schedule 8812 has one line for
both credits. DF splits it for its own explanations
(`/totalOdc`, `/totalCtc`; descriptions: "ODC credits are applied before CTC
credits as per the IRM and is also reduced first if there is a phase out"):
the ODC part is the ODC left after the whole phase-out, capped by line 14;
the rest is CTC. The split feeds no form line; `is_receiving_ctc` and
`is_receiving_odc` feed `ctc8862_required`. The same "ODC first" order is why
line 16a (the unused part of line 12) can be treated as unused CTC, capped
by line 16b.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # DF: /maxPotentialOdcAfterPhaseOut
  definition max_potential_odc_after_phase_out equals
    Money.positive of (total_potential_odc - dependent_credit_phaseout)

  # DF: /totalOdc
  definition total_odc equals
    if total_ctc_and_odc = $0 then $0
    else Money.min of max_potential_odc_after_phase_out, total_ctc_and_odc

  # DF: /totalCtc
  definition total_ctc equals
    if total_ctc_and_odc = $0 then $0
    else total_ctc_and_odc - total_odc

  # DF: /isReceivingCtc
  rule is_receiving_ctc under condition total_ctc > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  # DF: /isReceivingOdc
  rule is_receiving_odc under condition total_odc > $0
  consequence fulfilled
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(d), (h)(5), (h)(6): Part II-A, the additional child tax credit for all filers

IRC 24(d)(1): "The aggregate credits allowed to a taxpayer under subpart C
shall be increased by the lesser of— (A) the credit which would be allowed
under this section without regard to this subsection and the limitation under
section 26(a) or (B) the amount by which the aggregate amount of credits
allowed by this subpart (determined without regard to this subsection) would
increase if the limitation imposed by section 26(a) were increased by the
greater of— (i) 15 percent of so much of the taxpayer's earned income (within
the meaning of section 32) which is taken into account in computing taxable
income for the taxable year as exceeds $3,000, or (ii) in the case of a
taxpayer with 3 or more qualifying children, the excess (if any) of— (I) the
taxpayer's social security taxes for the taxable year, over (II) the credit
allowed under section 32 for the taxable year. ... For purposes of
subparagraph (B), any amount excluded from gross income by reason of section
112 shall be treated as earned income which is taken into account in
computing taxable income for the taxable year."

IRC 24(h)(5)(A): "The amount determined under subsection (d)(1)(A) with
respect to any qualifying child shall not exceed $1,400, and such subsection
shall be applied without regard to paragraph (4) of this subsection." Rev.
Proc. 2023-34 § 3.05 (p 8): "For taxable years beginning in 2024, the amount
used in § 24(d)(1)(A) to determine the amount of credit under § 24 that may be
refundable is $1,700." (`P.actc_per_qualifying_child_cap`). IRC 24(h)(6):
"Subsection (d)(1)(B)(i) shall be applied by substituting "$2,500" for
"$3,000"." (`P.actc_earned_income_floor`, rate `P.actc_earned_income_rate`).

Schedule 8812 line 16a: "Subtract line 14 from line 12. If zero, stop here;
you cannot take the additional child tax credit." Line 16b: "Number of
qualifying children under age 17 with the required social security number: x
$1,700. ... If zero, stop here". Line 17: "Enter the smaller of line 16a or
line 16b". Line 18a: "Earned income (see instructions)"; line 18b:
"Nontaxable combat pay". Line 19: "Is the amount on line 18a more than $2,500?
No. Leave line 19 blank and enter -0- on line 20. Yes. Subtract $2,500 from
the amount on line 18a." Line 20: "Multiply the amount on line 19 by 15%
(0.15)". "Next. On line 16b, is the amount $5,100 or more? No. ... skip Part
II-B and enter the smaller of line 17 or line 20 on line 27. Yes. If line 20
is equal to or more than line 17, skip Part II-B and enter the amount from
line 17 on line 27. Otherwise, go to line 21."

**Line 18a.** The Earned Income Chart (`i1040s8--2024.pdf` p 7): a filer
taking the EIC enters "your earned income from Step 5 of the EIC
instructions ..., plus all of your nontaxable combat pay if you did not elect
to include it in earned income for the EIC"; any other filer uses the Earned
Income Worksheet (p 8): line 1a "the amount from line 1z of Form 1040", plus
1b "nontaxable combat pay", less (lines 4 to 6) Medicaid waiver payments
excluded on Schedule 1 line 8s and Schedule 1 line 15 (self-employment).
In DF's scope there is no self-employment income, and the W-2 items that
make earned income differ from line 1z (box 11 nonqualified plans, box 12
code II Medicaid waiver payments) are knockouts (`formW2s.xml`
`/flowKnockoutNonQualifiedPlans`, `/formW2s/*/knockoutBox12Code`). Both
routes then give line 1z plus all combat pay: DF
`income.xml` `/earnedIncomeWithAllCombatPay` = `Round(employerIncomeSubtotal
+ allCombatPay)`. Section 112 (combat pay) is the "amount excluded from gross
income by reason of section 112" of 24(d)(1).

**The order of the two tests.** DF computes line 26 whenever there are three
or more qualifying children (`/maximumActc`: `GreaterOf(regularMaximumActc,
socialSecurityOverEitc)`), without the form's shortcut "If line 20 is equal
to or more than line 17, skip Part II-B". The shortcut never changes line
27: if line 20 is at least line 17, then line 26 (at least line 20) is too,
and line 27 is line 17 either way.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # Sch 8812 line 16a, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2. DF: /remainingCtcAndOdc
  definition remaining_ctc_and_odc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.positive of (dependent_credit_less_phaseout - total_ctc_and_odc))

  # Sch 8812 line 16a "If zero, stop here". DF: /xmlHasRemainingCtcAndOdc
  rule xml_has_remaining_ctc_and_odc under condition
    dependent_credit_not_fully_phased_out and remaining_ctc_and_odc > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(h)(5); Rev. Proc. 2023-34 §3.05, rp-23-34.pdf p 8; 24(g)(1);
  # Sch 8812 line 16b, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2. DF: /totalPotentialActc
  definition total_potential_actc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if ctc_odc_disqualified_for_improper_claims or not maybe_eligible_for_ctc
       then $0
       else P.actc_per_qualifying_child_cap * (decimal of ctc_eligible_dependents))

  # Sch 8812 line 16b "If zero, stop here". DF: /xmlHasPotentialActc
  rule xml_has_potential_actc under condition
    xml_has_remaining_ctc_and_odc and total_potential_actc > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(d)(1)(A), 24(h)(5)(A); Sch 8812 line 17, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /remainingPotentialActc
  definition remaining_potential_actc equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.min of remaining_ctc_and_odc, total_potential_actc)

  # IRC 24(d)(1) last sentence (section 112 combat pay); Sch 8812 line 18a,
  # f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2; Earned Income Chart and Worksheet,
  # i1040s8--2024.pdf pp 7-8. DF: income.xml /earnedIncomeWithAllCombatPay
  definition earned_income_with_all_combat_pay equals
    R.round_dollar of (employer_income_subtotal + all_combat_pay)

  # IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(i), 24(h)(6); Sch 8812 line 19, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /earnedIncomeAboveActcRefundabilityThreshold, /actcRefundabilityThreshold
  definition earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.positive of
         (earned_income_with_all_combat_pay - P.actc_earned_income_floor))

  # Sch 8812 line 19 "Yes". DF: /earnedIncomeExceedsActcRefundabilityThreshold
  rule earned_income_exceeds_actc_refundability_threshold under condition
    xml_has_potential_actc
    and earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(i); Sch 8812 line 20, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /regularMaximumActc (Round(line 19 x 15/100))
  definition regular_maximum_actc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (earned_income_above_actc_refundability_threshold
       * P.actc_earned_income_rate)

  # IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(ii) "3 or more qualifying children"; Sch 8812 line 20
  # "Next. On line 16b, is the amount $5,100 or more?".
  # DF: /threeOrMoreCtcEligibleDependents
  rule three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents under condition
    ctc_eligible_dependents >= actc_alternative_minimum_children
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /xmlThreeOrMoreCtcEligibleDependents
  rule xml_three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents under condition
    xml_has_potential_actc and three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents
  consequence fulfilled
```

### 26 U.S.C. § 24(d)(1)(B)(ii) and (d)(2): Part II-B, three or more qualifying children

IRC 24(d)(2)(A): "The term "social security taxes" means, with respect to any
taxpayer for any taxable year— (i) the amount of the taxes imposed by sections
3101 and 3201(a) on amounts received by the taxpayer during the calendar year
in which the taxable year begins, (ii) 50 percent of the taxes imposed by
section 1401 on the self-employment income of the taxpayer for the taxable
year, and (iii) 50 percent of the taxes imposed by section 3211(a) on amounts
received by the taxpayer during the calendar year in which the taxable year
begins." (d)(2)(B): "The term "social security taxes" shall not include any
taxes to the extent the taxpayer is entitled to a special refund of such
taxes under section 6413(c)."

Schedule 8812 line 21: "Withheld social security, Medicare, and Additional
Medicare taxes from Form(s) W-2, boxes 4 and 6. If married filing jointly,
include your spouse's amounts with yours." Line 22: "Enter the total of the
amounts from Schedule 1 (Form 1040), line 15; Schedule 2 (Form 1040), line 5;
Schedule 2 (Form 1040), line 6; and Schedule 2 (Form 1040), line 13". Line 23:
"Add lines 21 and 22". Line 24: "Enter the total of the amounts from Form 1040
or 1040-SR, line 27, and Schedule 3 (Form 1040), line 11." Line 25: "Subtract
line 24 from line 23. If zero or less, enter -0-". Line 26: "Enter the larger
of line 20 or line 25. Next, enter the smaller of line 17 or line 26 on line
27."

In DF's scope: line 21 is `/socialSecurityTaxesWithheld` (`Form_w2s`; boxes 4
and 6 of every W-2); line 22 is `$0` (no self-employment, no unreported tip
or wage tax: Schedule 2 lines 5, 6, 13 are out of scope); Schedule 3 line 11
(excess social security tax withheld, the 6413(c) special refund of
(d)(2)(B)) is a knockout (`Form_w2s.ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages`),
and so is a W-2 with Additional Medicare Tax or tier 1 RRTA tax. So line 25 is
`max(0, socialSecurityTaxesWithheld - earnedIncomeCredit)`: DF
`/socialSecurityOverEitc`.

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # OUT OF SCOPE: Sch 8812 line 22 (Schedule 1 line 15, Schedule 2 lines 5, 6,
  # 13) is $0 and Schedule 3 line 11 is a knockout (Form_w2s), see above.
  # IRC 24(d)(1)(B)(ii), 24(d)(2); Sch 8812 lines 21-25, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2.
  # DF: /socialSecurityOverEitc
  definition social_security_over_eitc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.positive of (social_security_taxes_withheld - earned_income_credit))

  # IRC 24(d)(1)(B); Sch 8812 line 26 (line 20 when Part II-B does not apply),
  # f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2. DF: /maximumActc
  definition maximum_actc equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (if three_or_more_ctc_eligible_dependents
       then Money.max of regular_maximum_actc, social_security_over_eitc
       else regular_maximum_actc)
```

### Part II-C: line 27

Schedule 8812 line 27: "This is your additional child tax credit. Enter this
amount on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 28." It is the smaller of line
17 and line 26 (or line 20).

```catala
scope Schedule8812:
  # IRC 24(d)(1); Sch 8812 line 27, f1040s8--2024.pdf p 2; Form 1040 line 28.
  # DF: /additionalCtc
  definition additional_ctc equals
    R.round_dollar of (Money.min of remaining_potential_actc, maximum_actc)

  # DF: /isReceivingActc
  rule is_receiving_actc under condition additional_ctc > $0
  consequence fulfilled
```
